      "text": "The script finds the first block (the monthly value-weighted table), parses each YYYYMM row, and computes 0.5\u00b7(SMALL LoPRIOR + BIG LoPRIOR) \u2212 0.5\u00b7(SMALL HiPRIOR + BIG HiPRIOR). Missing codes (-99.99 or -999) are treated as NaN, and any month whose inputs are missing is dropped.\n\n```python\nimport re\nimport math\nimport pandas as pd\n\nINPUT = \"6_Portfolios_ME_Prior_1_0.csv\"\nOUTPUT = \"output.csv\"\nHEADER_TAG = \"Average Value Weighted Returns -- Monthly\"\n\n\ndef to_num(tok):\n    try:\n        v = float(tok)\n    except ValueError:\n        return math.nan\n    if v == -99.99 or v == -999.0:\n        return math.nan\n    return v\n\n\ndef main():\n    with open(INPUT, encoding=\"latin-1\") as f:\n        lines = f.read().splitlines()\n\n    start = None\n    for i, line in enumerate(lines):\n        if HEADER_TAG in line:\n            start = i\n            break\n    if start is None:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Monthly value-weighted block not found\")\n\n    records = []\n    started = False\n    for line in lines[start + 1:]:\n        s = line.strip()\n        if not s:\n            if started:\n                break\n            continue\n        parts = [p.strip() for p in s.split(\",\")]\n        if re.fullmatch(r\"\\d{6}\", parts[0]) and len(parts) >= 7:\n            started = True\n            date = int(parts[0])\n            vals = [to_num(p) for p in parts[1:7]]\n            # order: SMALL LoPRIOR, ME1 PRIOR2, SMALL HiPRIOR,\n            #        BIG LoPRIOR, ME2 PRIOR2, BIG HiPRIOR\n            s_lo, s_hi, b_lo, b_hi = vals[0], vals[2], vals[3], vals[5]\n            value = 0.5 * (s_lo + b_lo) - 0.5 * (s_hi + b_hi)\n            if not math.isnan(value):\n                records.append((date, value))\n        else:\n            if started:\n                break\n\n    out = pd.DataFrame(records, columns=[\"date\", \"value\"])\n    out[\"date\"] = out[\"date\"].astype(int)\n    out.to_csv(OUTPUT, index=False)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
